      "type": "rectangle",
      "name": "Route behavior",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "Containers own their connections"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "Objects connect directly across containers. Collapsing a parent brings hidden child connections to its border; expanding restores them. Parent borders can also connect inward to children, as shown in the architecture bookmarks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "runs": [
            {
              "text": "Free lines below use explicit bend points. Endpoint markers cover arrows, bars, circles, triangles, diamonds, crow feet and cardinalities."
            }
          ]
        }
